    "title": "Quioccasin Middle School teacher receives \"Yay of the Day\" recognition",
    "text": "Crystal Alphin, a science teacher at Quioccasin Middle School, has been recognized as the latest “Yay of the Day” honoree. Superintendent Amy Cashwell presented the award to Alphin at Quioccasin.\nEmily Holloway-Costa, who nominated Alphin, said, “She made a chocolate chip pie for her class — it was a reward for having returned their signed syllabi quickly — and shared the recipe with families. She has been so responsive and thoughtful when we have reached out to her in these first few weeks, and as parents of a new middle schooler, we are deeply grateful.\n“She is already so impressive to us with her sweet motivational skills for her students and her fantastic communication with parents. We are so fortunate to have her!”\nThe “Yay of the Day” series highlights staff members who make positive contributions to Henrico County Public Schools. Community members can nominate staff for this recognition through the school division’s website at https://www.henricoschools.us/yay-of-the-day .",
